PHASE I: UEFI-ROOT AND RING -1 SUBSTRATE (A-HVS)\uc0\u8232 To eliminate the "fat and noisy" interference of standard kernels, Axion initializes as a UEFI DXE (Driver Execution Environment) driver during the early boot phase.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. Pre-Kernel Virtualization (VMX-Root)\
Axion takes control of the Global Descriptor Table (GDT) and Interrupt Descriptor Table (IDT) before the OS bootloader. It activates VMX-Root mode, creating a persistent Hyper-Isolator.\
Logic: The host OS is trapped in a non-root partition. Every hardware request from the OS (I/O, IRQ, MSR) is intercepted via VM-Exits. During high-velocity compute pulses, Axion forces the OS into a "Stall-Wait" state, ensuring zero bus-contention for the primary fabric.\
B. SMM-Jailing and SMI-Trap\
System Management Interrupts (SMIs) are invisible to the OS and cause catastrophic jitter. At the UEFI level, Axion locks the SMI-configuration to ensure all hardware-level interrupts are routed through the SMI-Trap.\
Equation 7: Jitter-Free Window (W_jf)\
W_jf = T_cycle - (T_SMM_delay + T_VM-Exit_overhead)\
