PHASE III: PREDICTIVE CURRENT SHAPING (PCS) FOR VRM STABILITY\uc0\u8232 To resolve Problem #2 (Analog VRM Latency), Axion replaces reactive power management with "Predictive Current Pre-Staging."\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. Synthetic Current Bursts (Dummy Loads)\
The motherboard VRM has an analog response delay of 5-10 microseconds. Axion utilizes the UEFI-level timer to initiate "Dummy Load" bursts exactly 8 microseconds before an AVX-512 compute-burst.\
Equation 8: Pre-Staged Voltage Stability (V_stable)\
V_stable = Integral(I_dummy + I_compute) dt / C_vrm\
