\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. Shadow-Core Sandbox Evolution (The Golden Path)\
To maintain absolute stability, ASEE operates via "Sandboxed Genetic Mutation."\
Logic: ASEE does not deploy new architectural optimizations directly to the production fabric. Instead, it utilizes a "Shadow Core" (an isolated execution unit) to run "Genetic Mutations" (new MOI/PCS/TGC configurations).\
Vetting Process: A mutation must survive a "Billion-Cycle Stress Test" within the Shadow-Core Sandbox. During this period, the HASL NMI-Guardian monitors for even a single nanosecond of jitter or 0.001C of thermal drift.\
Equation 14: Sandbox Stability Coefficient (S_sc)\
S_sc = (N_stable_cycles / 10^9) == 1.0\
Only when S_sc reaches 1.0 is the mutation promoted from the Shadow-Core to the Ring -1 Production Substrate.\
B. Hardware-Software Co-Evolution\
Equation 13: Evolutionary Gain (G_evo)\
G_evo = Delta_Throughput / Delta_Energy_per_Cycle\
By rewarding patterns that increase compute-density while decreasing thermal noise in the Sandbox, Axion evolves as a living, self-optimizing, and fundamentally stable organism.\
